      "message": "Considering the changes have enabled this on most platforms. I think it\u0027ll be best to separate dfu_bootmanager.c and CONFIG_DFU_BOOTMANAGER into their shared and main components.\n\ndfu_bootmanager.c would split into dfu_bootmanager_main.c and dfu_bootmanager_shared.c with the backup memory operations moved to the shared file.\n\nThe RO region would have CONFIG_DFU_BOOTMANAGER_MAIN since this behavior conflicts with some of the existing ifneq $(CONFIG_COMMON_RUNTIME) evaluations and we likely can\u0027t make assumptions that CONFIG_COMMON_RUNTIME is always enabled in the RW. Both regions would enable the CONFIG_DFU_BOOTMANAGER_SHARED define which has few conflicts by itself assuming there are available backup registers.\n\nAre there any concerns about this change?",
